I'm a software developer based in Western North Carolina, currently a Founding Engineer at [Membrane](https://membrane.io) where we're building a platform for programmable tools and automations.

Most of my day-to-day is spent writing Rust and TypeScript. Lately, I've been having fun learning more about WASM, containers, and JS runtimes.

Outside of programming I [climb](https://www.mountainproject.com/user/200179390/thomas-seeley), [backpack](/tags/trip-report/), and [travel](/tags/trip-report/) when I can.

You can find me on [GitHub][gh], [Codeberg][cb], [Tangled][tg], [Bluesky][bs], [Mastodon][ms], and [X][x], or reach me at [hello@tseeley.com](mailto:hello@tseeley.com).

